# The API is a Netlify Function. Netlify evaluates these rules before it
# looks for a function, so the SPA fallback alone would swallow every
# /api/* request and answer with the app shell instead of the provider.
/api/*    /.netlify/functions/api/:splat   200

# The app is a single page: every path serves the same document, and the
# client reads its state from the query string. Netlify serves
# /assets/* and /cesium/* as static files first, so this rule only catches
# what is left.
/*    /index.html   200
